'''Turtwig''' ([[List of Japanese Pokémon names|Japanese]]: '''ナエトル''' ''Naetle'') is a {{type|Grass}} {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} introduced in [[Generation IV]].

It [[Evolution|evolves]] into {{p|Grotle}} starting at [[level]] 18, which evolves into {{p|Torterra}} starting at [[level]] 32.

Along with {{p|Chimchar}} and {{p|Piplup}}, Turtwig is one of the three [[Sinnoh first partner Pokémon|first partner Pokémon of Sinnoh]] available at the beginning of {{game|Diamond and Pearl|s|Pokémon Diamond, Pearl}}, {{v2|Platinum}}, {{pkmn|Brilliant Diamond and Shining Pearl|Brilliant Diamond, and Shining Pearl}}.

==Biology==
[[File:Turtwig wilting.png|thumb|220px|left|A Turtwig tired from thirst, with its leaf wilting]]
Turtwig is a small, light green, quadrupedal {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} resembling a {{wp|turtle}} or {{wp|tortoise}}. Its eyes, feet, and lower jaw are yellow. Its body is covered by a brown shell that is composed of earth and minerals. The shell has a thick black stripe and a black rim. On a very healthy Turtwig, the shell should feel moist. A pair of small leaves, described singularly as "the leaf on its head" by the [[Pokédex]], grow on a brown patch on its head. This leaf will wilt if the Pokémon becomes thirsty.

Since it is a plant-based Pokémon, Turtwig usually nourishes itself through photosynthesis; it becomes more energetic when exposed to enough sunlight. It also drinks water, which hardens its soil-based shell. Due to its status as a first partner Pokémon, a wild Turtwig is hard to come by and it is generally found under the ownership of {{pkmn|Trainer}}s. It has been recently seen living in the [[Terarium]] of [[Blueberry Academy]].
