==Other appearances==
Turtwig appears in [[Super Smash Bros. Brawl]] as a trophy.

===Trophy information===
''"A Tiny Leaf Pokémon. Despite its animal appearance, Turtwig actually has vegetation sprouting from its head. The shell on its back is made of soil and hardens when it drinks water. Much like a plant, Turtwig performs photosynthesis, absorbing sunlight and making oxygen. It also relies heavily on water to keep its plant healthy and thus spends a lot of time near lakes. Turtwig evolves into Grotle."''

==Trivia==
* Turtwig is the heaviest of the basic forms of all of the [[first partner Pokémon]]. It also has the lowest base {{stat|Speed}} stat out of all first partner Pokémon.
* Turtwig is the only first partner Pokémon to know {{m|Withdraw|a stat-raising move}} when initially received as a {{player}}'s first Pokémon.
* Turtwig is the only {{t|Grass}} type first partner Pokémon to learn a {{t|Water}} type move by level up, that being {{m|Withdraw}}.

===Origin===
{{Bulbanews|On the Origin of Species: Turtwig, Grotle and Torterra}}
Turtwig seems to be based on a terrestrial {{wp|turtle}}, possibly one of the {{wp|Asian box turtle|Asian box turtles}}. In concept, it may be based on the {{wp|World Turtle}} from various mythologies that carries the world upon its back.

====Name origin====
Turtwig may be a combination of ''{{wp|turtle}}'' and ''twig''.

Naetle may be a combination of 苗 ''nae'' ({{wp|Sprouting|sprout}}) and ''turtle''.

